  "question": {
    "text": "A particle experiences a variable force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math> in a horizontal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> plane. Assume distance in meters and force is newton. If the particle moves from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> plane, then Kinetic Energy changes by :"
